{
  // Relief check (BIOMEGEN.md 13 phases A to D: highlands, linear mountain ranges, massifs and
  // lone peaks, islands and archipelagos, great lakes): run from
  // OpenGLTest/ with
  //   VOXEL_TIME=1090 VOXEL_SCRIPT=visual-examples/terrain-shape.json
  // Shots land in visual/terrain-shape/. The whole run takes about eight minutes of clock, far
  // longer than the afternoon after noon (147) lasts, so it starts at 1090, which is -110 one
  // 1200 s day later, 43 s after sunrise (about 1047): the first shot lands near 1108, with the
  // sun up, the middle ones around noon (1347), and the last near 1585, before sunset (about
  // 1647). The scene is only brightly lit from about 1080 to 1610, so the run has to fit in about
  // 530 s: Phase C's five shots moved the start down from 1160, and phase D's six shots cut the
  // waits instead (20 s after a long hop, 6 s within one lake; 22 s instead of 30 for the earlier
  // non-vista shots, 25 for the vistas), since at 1090 with the old waits the last three
  // great-lake shots fell after sunset and an earlier start leaves the first ones in the dawn.
  // Starting at 147 instead leaves the later shots in dusk and night.
  //
  // The vantage points come from a headless probe over TerrainRelief.HighlandWeight,
  // TerrainRelief.MountainHeight, RangeLattice and RangeDirection, WaterBodies.RiverWeight and
  // TerrainGenerator.LandHeight (default seed):
  //   origin_valley    - the spawn, inside ReliefSpawnClear: highland weight 0, so the land is the
  //                      forest valley it was before the relief layer (ground 12)
  //   forest_highland  - a wet-forest highland interior at weight 1 with no range and an open forest
  //                      (ForestOpenness 1) around (-3367, 2084) (ground 50), from about 60 blocks up:
  //                      lifted, broken hill country with valleys between, not spikes
  //   range_along      - a forest range in range cell (0, 2), whose hashed direction is (0.58, 0.81)
  //                      (yaw 54); the crest runs through (1050, 3635), (1191, 3870) and (1238, 3917)
  //                      at ground 60-70 and stays above 15 blocks of range over 900 of 1200 blocks
  //                      along that line. Filmed from its south-west end looking along it
  //   range_across     - the same range from 300 blocks off its side, looking across it (yaw 144)
  //   arid_plateau     - a steppe highland at weight 1 around (-4025, -4119) (ground 25-29, steppe and
  //                      weight 1 for 120 blocks around): the
  //                      arid hill reduction still flattens it, so it reads as a lifted plateau
  //   highland_border  - a forest lowland at (-1465, 4833) (weight 0, ground 21) looking north-north-
  //                      west (yaw 107) at the highland rising 300 blocks away (weight 1, ground 33)
  //   river_wash       - a river at (-3000, 3240) in the lowland (forest floor 13, level 0) looking
  //                      (yaw -146) up its channel toward (-3304, 3032), where the floor climbs to 36
  //                      inside a highland, past RiverLowEnd, so the channel dries into a wash
  //   range_cell_border - a taiga range crossing a range-cell border at (-30, 4387) (blend 0.45),
  //                      from high above: the cell borders are jittered (MountainRangeCellWarp), so
  //                      no straight north-south or east-west seam may show where the range turns
  //   lod_vista        - a high view over the forest highland across the full-detail ring into the
  //                      far LOD, for over-dark far valleys (LodSkyExposure)
  // Phase B (hashed peaks, TerrainPeaks), from a headless probe over TerrainPeaks.MassifSiteAt,
  // PeakSiteAt and TerrainGenerator.LandHeight (default seed). Inside +-6000 there are two accepted
  // massifs: cell (0, -4), center (1131, -4900), radius 256, rise 89.8, crown land 120.6 at
  // (1119, -4932), forest; and cell (0, -2), center (997, -2777), radius 179, crown 121.7, steppe.
  // The shots use the first:
  //   massif_far       - from 500 blocks west (ground 16) looking east (yaw 0) at the whole silhouette
  //                      and its wobbled outline
  //   massif_flank     - 210 blocks south of the center at y 75 (the flank ground there is about 25)
  //                      looking up the south flank: spurs, bare rock above MountainRockHeight and
  //                      snow toward MountainSnowFullHeight
  //   massif_summit    - 58 blocks south of the crown at y 140 (below the cloud layer at 160) looking
  //                      down onto the snow-capped crown
  //   lone_peak        - the lone peak at (-2721, 3061) (radius 67, height 46, top 61 over a plain whose
  //                      rim spreads 13..18) from 150 blocks west (ground 13)
  //   massif_lod_vista - from 900 blocks west at y 150, across the full-detail ring onto the massif in
  //                      the far LOD, for LOD holes and over-dark far valleys beside it
  // No other scenario's teleport farther than 1536 blocks from the origin lies within 64 blocks of a
  // massif or a lone peak.
  // Phase C (islands and archipelagos, TerrainIslands), from a headless probe over
  // BiomeClassifier.PreIslandOceanWeight and BiomeWeights (island land: the pre-island ocean weight
  // past OceanShoreWeight, the folded one under it), TerrainIslands.TryGetArchipelago,
  // FootprintWeight and ArchipelagoWeight, TerrainGenerator.LandHeight and ColumnCache.Get (default
  // seed). The islands below have no continental dry land within 100 blocks:
  //   island_far       - a large island centered near (4617, 4) (core x 4368..4776, z -120..120),
  //                      highest at (4752, -72) (LandHeight 36.5, forest; its west end is savanna
  //                      and desert, stone pines and cacti on sand), from 250 blocks off its west
  //                      shore at y 40 looking east (yaw 0)
  //   island_beach     - low (y 6.5) over deep water off the same island's west shore at
  //                      (4325, -75), looking north (yaw 85) along the sand terraces of its rim
  //   island_knoll     - a small knoll centered near (5572, 20) (core 16 blocks across, highest 4.0,
  //                      forest: a sand knoll under one tree), from 50 blocks south-west at y 8.5
  //                      (yaw 51)
  //   archipelago_chain - the accepted archipelago in cell (2, 1): center (3776, 2601), half length
  //                      761, half width 259, direction yaw -28, a taiga chain of islands at 371 and
  //                      83 blocks before the center and at it (highest 38.7, 28.7 and 10.2) set in
  //                      pack ice; from y 140 at (3158, 2929), 685 blocks before the center, looking
  //                      along the chain (pitch -25)
  //   island_lod_vista - from 900 blocks west of the large island at y 150 (yaw 0), across the
  //                      full-detail ring onto it and its neighbors in the far LOD, for LOD holes,
  //                      floating LOD and a dry, sunken ring around an island at range
  // The same probe audited every other scenario's teleports farther than 1536 blocks from the
  // origin: only icebergs.json and biomes.json's pack_ice / pack_ice_low stand within 64 blocks of
  // island land (an island now rises just west of the iceberg row, around (-1100, -2510)). Both
  // were re-run: the bergs, the push and the pack-ice gradient still read, so they carry a note
  // instead of a move.
  // Phase D (great lakes, GreatLakes), from a headless probe over GreatLakes.SiteAt and Sample,
  // WaterBodies.RiverWeight, TerrainGenerator.BiomeAt and ColumnCache.Get (default seed). The
  // nearest accepted lakes past the spawn clearing are cell (4, 3) (three lobes, river-fed at
  // SeaLevel 0, center (5773, 4397), lobe radii 148/74/95, Frozen, so it is iced over), cell
  // (-6, -5) (one lobe of radius 179 at (-7322, -6252), river-fed at 0, forest) and cell (-8, -8)
  // (rim-fed at surface 8 with banks at 11..15, lobes (-9341, -9791) R 128 and (-9340, -9725) R 78,
  // an island of radius 60 at (-9340, -9789) whose ground stands at 15, forest). The lobed lakes
  // in reach, (4, 3) and (-4, 10), are both frozen, so the bay is the neck of (-8, -8)'s north lobe:
  //   great_lake_river     - the river that runs into lake (4, 3) from the north-east, joining it
  //                          near (5873, 4345); both iced at the one level 0, from its bank at y 30
  //   great_lake_lod_vista - from 330 blocks west of lake (-6, -5) at y 150 (yaw 0): its near half
  //                          is chunk water and its far half lies past the full-detail ring in the
  //                          far LOD, so the two sheets must meet without a step
  //   great_lake_shore     - on the east bank of lake (-8, -8) (ground 11, water 8) looking west
  //                          over the water to the island
  //   great_lake_island    - the island from y 40 north-east of the lake
  //   great_lake_bay       - from the north end at y 40 looking south into the narrower north lobe
  //   great_lake_height    - 80 blocks over the surface south of the lake, looking down onto the
  //                          whole outline, its terraced banks and the island
  // The same probe audited every scenario's teleports: none lies within 400 blocks of a great lake.
  // The camera flies (so it hovers instead of falling), every teleport is followed by a wait while
